  <article class="prose page">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p>
      I'm Gian — a research engineer working on high-performance AI systems, with
      about seven years spent taking machine learning from prototype to production.
      I'm currently co-founder and CTO at <strong>Unakin</strong>, where I've led
      LLM fine-tuning, shipped semantic search and inference into production for
      enterprise partners, and built the evaluation and training infrastructure
      underneath it — mostly distributed across A100 clusters in PyTorch.
    </p>

    <p>
      Most of my work lives at the boundary between models and the hardware they
      run on: FSDP, DDP and tensor parallelism for training at scale; custom
      Triton kernels when the standard ops leave memory or throughput on the table;
      and high-throughput serving on the inference side. One kernel I'm fond of cut
      cross-entropy memory in half and let us double the batch size — the kind of
      change that pays for itself every step of training.
    </p>

    <p>
      Before all this I was a physicist. I did my PhD in particle physics at Oxford
      and Royal Holloway, based largely at CERN, building distributed Monte Carlo
      simulations of particle interactions and detector response across compute
      clusters and validating them against experimental data. I was a core
      contributor to
      <a href="https://github.com/jairhul/pyg4ometry">pyg4ometry</a>, an
      open-source geometry library still used across high-energy physics, and I
      published a fair number of papers along the way. That background is where my
      instinct for numerical rigor and large-scale systems comes from.
    </p>

    <p>
      This site is my notebook for the systems side of ML — the parts that are hard
      to find written down clearly. Expect posts on distributed training internals,
      GPU kernels, and the unglamorous engineering that makes models fast and
      reliable in production.
    </p>

    <p>
      You can find me on
      <a href="https://github.com/gian-g3dai">GitHub</a> and
      <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/giandalessandro">LinkedIn</a>, or reach me at
      <a href="mailto:gianluigidalessandro23@gmail.com">gianluigidalessandro23@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
